GOA patch for TyrQuake (libretro) 67db338ff4d27fdbcead61d4e54938d758ae62cb: gamepad look-spring, centre view and gyro
look.

Upstream IN_Move calls V_StopPitchDrift() on every frame while a gamepad is the input device, whatever the right
stick is doing, so nothing can level the view: the centerview command, the lookspring option and Quake's
walk-forward recentring are all cancelled in the frame they start. This holds the drift off only while the right
stick is pitching the view (outside the analog deadzone), as the mouse and the look keys do, and with lookspring on
starts Quake's own recentring once the stick has rested for 0.6 s after looking up or down (the stick counterpart
of releasing mlook with lookspring on).

Upstream also reads the mouse only when the keyboard is the input device, so a gamepad player's frontend has no way
to add motion aiming (a phone's gyro). This applies mouse motion in the gamepad branch too, as the keyboard branch
does (m_yaw, m_pitch, sensitivity). Pitching that way stops the centring drift as the mouse does (the drift keeps
pulling the view level after it gets there), except that a tremor never cuts a centring short, and by more than a
tremor while the look-spring waits it calls the spring off, so the view stays where the tilt aims it.

